2.2.m:
Brahmā said:
Having reflected thus, Śivā remembered that Maheśa in her mind;
then, having obtained Śiva's permission, Durgā said to me at that time:

Nārada said:
Proper is your speech, dear father, sinless one who knows all;
truly, the wonderful, auspicious story of the two Śivas has been heard by us.

Brahmā said:
Having thus spoken the rule of righteousness, she felt remorse;
she remembered the words of Śaṅkara with an aching heart.

Viṣṇu said:
"For those wishing to prosper, no [harm] has ever been committed against a more fiery one;
for those who have done wrong, the wish to prosper is for the sake of well-being in many ways.
